We examine the approximation of entire functions through a sequence of operators that translate functions.
  \begin{equation*}
  \mathcal{L}_n(f)(z)=\frac{1}{2\pi i}\int_{\Gamma} \frac{f(w)}{w}
  \frac{w-z}{\sqrt{(w-z)^2+4n}}dz,
  \end{equan
We investigate under what conditions a given sequence of operators $\mathcal{L}_n$ can approximate any entire function $f$.
